From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: explorer: the animations switch is read where Windows keeps it

Task View's fly-in (0520) and the desktop slide (0521) asked
SPI_GETCLIENTAREAANIMATION, which Wine caches per process: turning animations
off in Settings (another process) went unseen until explorer restarted. They
read UserPreferencesMask (byte 4, 0x02) instead, as Settings' Effects page does.

Gate: make test-desktop-slide.
--- a/programs/explorer/vdesktop.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/vdesktop.c
@@ -643,9 +643,15 @@
 
 static BOOL tv_animations(void)
 {
-    BOOL on = TRUE;
-    if (!SystemParametersInfoW( SPI_GETCLIENTAREAANIMATION, 0, &on, 0 )) on = TRUE;
-    return on;
+    /* where Windows keeps it (UserPreferencesMask, byte 4, 0x02): Wine caches
+     * SPI values per process, so Settings turning animations off went unseen
+     * here until explorer restarted */
+    BYTE mask[16];
+    DWORD size = sizeof(mask);
+    if (RegGetValueW( HKEY_CURRENT_USER, L"Control Panel\\Desktop", L"UserPreferencesMask", RRF_RT_REG_BINARY,
+                      NULL, mask, &size ) || size < 5)
+        return TRUE;
+    return (mask[4] & 0x02) != 0;
 }
 
